1
00:00:00,959 --> 00:00:03,169
♪ <i>Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

2
00:00:03,253 --> 00:00:07,048
["Mr. Tailor" playing]

3
00:00:09,134 --> 00:00:10,802
♪ <i>Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

4
00:00:10,885 --> 00:00:12,929
♪ <i>Holding the scissors</i> ♪

5
00:00:13,012 --> 00:00:16,641
♪ <i>One cut, and it's settled</i> ♪

6
00:00:16,725 --> 00:00:19,769
[Red] <i>How do we get Ibyang from Atoy?</i>

7
00:00:19,853 --> 00:00:22,021
[Martina] We need to find someone

8
00:00:22,105 --> 00:00:24,649
who can pretend
to be Ibyang's real mother.

9
00:00:24,733 --> 00:00:25,817
What? An actress?

10
00:00:25,900 --> 00:00:26,860
[Martina, in English] <i>Something like that.</i>

11
00:00:26,943 --> 00:00:28,653
Mom, wake up, Mom!

12
00:00:28,737 --> 00:00:31,406
[in English] I'm Olga Bonifacio.
Olga, for short.

13
00:00:31,489 --> 00:00:35,493
Pretend you gave up
your child for adoption.

14
00:00:35,577 --> 00:00:37,203
[Red] <i>Then after a long time,</i>

15
00:00:37,287 --> 00:00:40,874
<i>you meet again and want to reunite.</i>

16
00:00:40,957 --> 00:00:42,041
[sobs] My child…

17
00:00:42,125 --> 00:00:43,376
It's me.

18
00:00:44,836 --> 00:00:46,838
It's me, your mama.

19
00:00:47,422 --> 00:00:49,924
I want to make it up to you
if you'll let me.

20
00:00:50,008 --> 00:00:52,177
- [in English] Cut.
- [Charmi] <i>Um, Ms. Ame?</i>

21
00:00:52,260 --> 00:00:55,013
Where can we meet Ibyang?

22
00:00:55,096 --> 00:00:59,184
So we can bring her mother to you.

23
00:00:59,267 --> 00:01:00,727
What's her name?

24
00:01:01,311 --> 00:01:02,979
[Charmi] <i>Olga Bonifacio.</i>

25
00:01:03,063 --> 00:01:04,856
You know, this place looks familiar to me.

26
00:01:04,939 --> 00:01:06,483
[vocal exercising]

27
00:01:07,859 --> 00:01:08,943
- [Atoy] <i>Olga?</i>
- [Ame] <i>Atoy!</i>

28
00:01:09,027 --> 00:01:10,445
[Ame] <i>She's Ibyang's mother!</i>

29
00:01:10,528 --> 00:01:11,446
[Atoy] <i>Her?</i>

30
00:01:11,529 --> 00:01:12,906
How did you meet?

31
00:01:14,074 --> 00:01:15,116
- [Atoy] <i>Oh.</i>
- [Olga] <i>Oh, what's that? Oh!</i>

32
00:01:15,200 --> 00:01:16,451
- [Olga] <i>What--</i>
- [Atoy] <i>Oh, sorry-- Oh!</i>

33
00:01:16,534 --> 00:01:17,952
- [in English] Sorry. Sorry.
- What's that?

34
00:01:18,036 --> 00:01:19,454
PREVIOUSLY

35
00:01:19,537 --> 00:01:20,830
[Olga] <i>What's your name?</i>

36
00:01:20,914 --> 00:01:22,123
Uh, Atoy.

37
00:01:22,207 --> 00:01:23,666
Do you have a girlfriend?

38
00:01:23,750 --> 00:01:25,585
Aren't you moving a bit too fast, miss?

39
00:01:25,668 --> 00:01:26,544
Don't you want us

40
00:01:26,628 --> 00:01:28,671
- to get to know each other first?
- What else do you want to know?

41
00:01:28,755 --> 00:01:30,590
[music swells]

42
00:01:31,174 --> 00:01:32,467
♪ <i>Fix this</i> ♪

43
00:01:32,550 --> 00:01:34,219
[music fades]

44
00:01:35,470 --> 00:01:37,639
- She approached me.
- Destiny.

45
00:01:38,223 --> 00:01:39,265
- What?
- [quirky sting]

46
00:01:39,349 --> 00:01:41,935
- Well, we bumped into each other
- [sneaky music playing]

47
00:01:42,018 --> 00:01:45,104
while I was looking for the church
of San Antonio de Padua.

48
00:01:45,772 --> 00:01:48,900
I thought he was the answer to my prayers,

49
00:01:48,983 --> 00:01:51,152
but… nothing.

50
00:01:51,236 --> 00:01:52,821
- He ghosted me.
- Huh?

51
00:01:52,904 --> 00:01:55,949
How could I call you?
The number got erased from my palm.

52
00:01:56,032 --> 00:01:57,909
Why did you write it on my palm?

53
00:01:57,992 --> 00:01:58,952
Of course it would get erased!

54
00:01:59,786 --> 00:02:01,663
- Oh.
- Excuses, my God.

55
00:02:01,746 --> 00:02:03,540
You should've remembered it.

56
00:02:03,623 --> 00:02:07,335
Okay? Or… at least looked for me.

57
00:02:07,418 --> 00:02:09,170
Right? Around.

58
00:02:09,254 --> 00:02:12,006
You know, if you want something,
you'll find a way,

59
00:02:12,090 --> 00:02:14,342
and that's what
I'm doing now to see my child.

60
00:02:14,425 --> 00:02:15,677
Ah.

61
00:02:15,760 --> 00:02:17,637
[sneaky music playing]

62
00:02:17,720 --> 00:02:18,680
Where is she?

63
00:02:18,763 --> 00:02:20,390
[scoffs]

64
00:02:20,473 --> 00:02:23,017
- Is this her room?
- Wait, wait, wait, wait, wait.

65
00:02:23,101 --> 00:02:24,269
What now?

66
00:02:27,313 --> 00:02:30,358
How can I be sure
you're really Ibyang's mother?

67
00:02:31,276 --> 00:02:33,403
As far as I know…

68
00:02:33,486 --> 00:02:34,779
[suspicious music playing]

69
00:02:36,322 --> 00:02:39,450
…her parent's name is Martin.

70
00:02:39,534 --> 00:02:42,036
[suspicious music playing]

71
00:02:42,120 --> 00:02:43,621
[Martina, in English]
<i>You need to watch out for Atoy.</i>

72
00:02:43,705 --> 00:02:45,039
He's Ibyang's guardian,

73
00:02:45,123 --> 00:02:47,542
and he's not very easily convinced.

74
00:02:48,126 --> 00:02:51,212
Atoy. That name sounds familiar.

75
00:02:52,213 --> 00:02:54,007
Don't worry, madam.

76
00:02:54,090 --> 00:02:56,259
My friend's charm is something else.

77
00:02:56,342 --> 00:02:58,553
That Atoy, he'll fold. Right?

78
00:02:59,178 --> 00:03:00,096
He should.

79
00:03:00,179 --> 00:03:02,724
[in English] I mean,
you're getting paid well enough.

80
00:03:09,647 --> 00:03:10,481
‪[inaudible]

81
00:03:11,232 --> 00:03:12,191
- [Red] Oh.
- Oh.

82
00:03:12,275 --> 00:03:13,109
This is the complete amount

83
00:03:13,192 --> 00:03:14,152
- for the first month.
- [in English] Thank you, sir.

84
00:03:14,235 --> 00:03:15,361
Thank you.

85
00:03:16,654 --> 00:03:19,657
Remember, do your job well.

86
00:03:20,283 --> 00:03:21,409
That's big money.

87
00:03:21,492 --> 00:03:23,912
So, there's no backing out,

88
00:03:23,995 --> 00:03:26,289
and do everything we tell you properly,

89
00:03:26,372 --> 00:03:27,999
because if not,

90
00:03:28,583 --> 00:03:30,043
I'll bury you alive.

91
00:03:30,126 --> 00:03:31,711
[music fades]

92
00:03:31,794 --> 00:03:34,005
Really? Oh.

93
00:03:34,088 --> 00:03:35,840
Ah-- Just kidding.

94
00:03:35,924 --> 00:03:37,383
- [Olga chuckles]
- My comedy is dark.

95
00:03:37,467 --> 00:03:38,301
[both chuckling]

96
00:03:39,802 --> 00:03:41,429
[sinister music playing]

97
00:03:42,180 --> 00:03:45,350
As long as the money keeps coming,

98
00:03:45,433 --> 00:03:47,310
consider it done.

99
00:03:47,393 --> 00:03:48,645
[music fades]

100
00:03:49,604 --> 00:03:51,189
[in English] Excuse me?

101
00:03:51,272 --> 00:03:52,607
[sighs]

102
00:03:53,191 --> 00:03:57,070
Just because you saw
"Martin" written down,

103
00:03:57,153 --> 00:03:59,656
doesn't mean I'm fake, okay?

104
00:03:59,739 --> 00:04:00,573
‪[scoffs]

105
00:04:01,741 --> 00:04:03,284
Martin is my ex.

106
00:04:04,535 --> 00:04:06,162
He's Ibyang's real father.

107
00:04:06,246 --> 00:04:08,289
[suspicious music playing]

108
00:04:09,082 --> 00:04:10,041
What?

109
00:04:11,542 --> 00:04:12,835
Are you sure?

110
00:04:12,919 --> 00:04:16,005
Well, if you don't believe me,
do a DNA test.

111
00:04:16,089 --> 00:04:17,590
But you'll pay, okay?

112
00:04:18,132 --> 00:04:20,093
- It's expensive. It's really expensive.
- [Charmi] Right?

113
00:04:20,176 --> 00:04:24,055
Oh, Atoy, Sister Norma
already gave her blessing.

114
00:04:24,138 --> 00:04:25,807
Even her niece is here.

115
00:04:29,644 --> 00:04:30,979
[Olga] Atoy.

116
00:04:31,980 --> 00:04:36,109
I know I made a big mistake
leaving Ibyang with Sister Norma.

117
00:04:36,192 --> 00:04:38,194
[melancholic music playing]

118
00:04:38,278 --> 00:04:41,864
But what could I do?

119
00:04:43,241 --> 00:04:46,911
I had no money, no job.

120
00:04:48,871 --> 00:04:50,790
I know I was a bad mother.

121
00:04:54,585 --> 00:04:58,339
But now, I want to make up for it.

122
00:04:58,423 --> 00:05:01,342
That's why I'm working hard
to have my own house,

123
00:05:01,426 --> 00:05:02,969
to start a business.

124
00:05:04,429 --> 00:05:06,723
I'm even taking side jobs,

125
00:05:06,806 --> 00:05:09,225
so I can have a career as an actress.

126
00:05:09,309 --> 00:05:10,768
Oh, you know, that's possible.

127
00:05:10,852 --> 00:05:13,271
You're beautiful. Ibyang takes after you.

128
00:05:18,609 --> 00:05:20,528
Not a day passed
that I didn't think of her.

129
00:05:22,864 --> 00:05:24,574
I searched for her for so long.

130
00:05:25,616 --> 00:05:26,492
So, I hope

131
00:05:26,576 --> 00:05:30,121
you'll let me see the child.

132
00:05:32,206 --> 00:05:37,045
[music turns dramatic]

133
00:05:47,055 --> 00:05:48,097
[music fades]

134
00:05:48,181 --> 00:05:50,433
[suave theme music playing]

135
00:05:52,769 --> 00:05:54,604
[motorcycle revving]

136
00:05:54,687 --> 00:05:56,522
[sewing machine whirring]

137
00:05:56,606 --> 00:05:58,524
[snipping]

138
00:05:59,150 --> 00:06:00,985
[sewing machine clacking]

139
00:06:02,487 --> 00:06:03,404
[gun cocks]

140
00:06:03,488 --> 00:06:05,782
[gunshots]

141
00:06:05,865 --> 00:06:08,076
[gunshots]

142
00:06:08,159 --> 00:06:10,161
[snipping]

143
00:06:14,540 --> 00:06:16,250
[electronic blipping]

144
00:06:17,418 --> 00:06:19,253
[music fades]

145
00:06:22,131 --> 00:06:23,549
‪[footsteps approaching]

146
00:06:28,262 --> 00:06:30,431
Oh, drink some water first.

147
00:06:30,515 --> 00:06:33,017
- Oh, thank you.
- She's coming down.

148
00:06:41,734 --> 00:06:42,693
[Atoy] Ibyang.

149
00:06:49,575 --> 00:06:52,954
[melodramatic music playing]

150
00:07:00,878 --> 00:07:02,463
She's Olga.

151
00:07:05,675 --> 00:07:07,009
She's your mother.

152
00:07:23,317 --> 00:07:24,569
My child…

153
00:07:26,612 --> 00:07:29,991
- [sentimental music playing]
- [gasping]

154
00:07:33,828 --> 00:07:36,247
[music fades]

155
00:07:37,165 --> 00:07:38,624
There.

156
00:07:38,708 --> 00:07:39,834
[in English] Prettiness.

157
00:07:39,917 --> 00:07:40,918
[soft chuckle]

158
00:07:41,002 --> 00:07:43,421
[somber music playing]

159
00:07:43,504 --> 00:07:46,549
Are you really my mama?

160
00:07:46,632 --> 00:07:49,093
[melancholic music playing]

161
00:07:49,177 --> 00:07:50,344
Yes, child.

162
00:07:56,559 --> 00:07:59,145
Why did you leave me?

163
00:08:04,609 --> 00:08:06,986
Because your mother was foolish. [inhales]

164
00:08:09,447 --> 00:08:12,617
I was afraid
I couldn't give you a good life.

165
00:08:15,036 --> 00:08:18,539
I knew you'd suffer more
if you were with me.

166
00:08:22,752 --> 00:08:25,421
But I'm suffering too.

167
00:08:27,882 --> 00:08:29,383
[music fades]

168
00:08:29,467 --> 00:08:31,135
Good thing

169
00:08:32,887 --> 00:08:35,640
kind people took care of me.

170
00:08:36,974 --> 00:08:39,268
Did you give me away because…

171
00:08:41,145 --> 00:08:44,106
- you didn't love me?
- Oh my. No, no.

172
00:08:44,190 --> 00:08:46,359
It wasn't like that, child. My child…

173
00:08:48,819 --> 00:08:50,112
It wasn't like that.

174
00:08:50,696 --> 00:08:51,781
I love you.

175
00:08:55,493 --> 00:08:57,078
When you love someone…

176
00:08:58,120 --> 00:09:01,290
[sobs] you don't give them away.

177
00:09:01,374 --> 00:09:04,752
[sobbing]

178
00:09:04,835 --> 00:09:08,297
[Olga] Forgive me, my child.
Mommy made a mistake.

179
00:09:10,675 --> 00:09:12,760
But I'm here now.

180
00:09:12,843 --> 00:09:14,762
We'll be together.

181
00:09:15,638 --> 00:09:17,932
[sobs] And if you'll agree…

182
00:09:19,517 --> 00:09:20,893
we'll go home.

183
00:09:22,436 --> 00:09:23,688
[melodramatic music playing]

184
00:09:23,771 --> 00:09:26,148
If you're going to take me…

185
00:09:28,359 --> 00:09:31,654
can it be the day after tomorrow instead?

186
00:09:32,530 --> 00:09:36,534
I want to spend time
with Sis Ame and Tatoy.

187
00:09:41,747 --> 00:09:42,915
Okay.

188
00:09:50,548 --> 00:09:53,259
[music swells]

189
00:09:53,342 --> 00:09:58,723
[music turns dramatic]

190
00:10:11,360 --> 00:10:13,112
- Oh my.
- [Charmi] Oh?

191
00:10:14,363 --> 00:10:16,741
What happened?
Why aren't you with the child?

192
00:10:16,824 --> 00:10:20,202
She said she still wants to spend time
with Ame and Atoy for a while.

193
00:10:20,870 --> 00:10:24,498
You know, I'm nervous, like…

194
00:10:25,082 --> 00:10:25,958
I can't relax.

195
00:10:26,042 --> 00:10:27,710
Oh. Why?

196
00:10:28,711 --> 00:10:30,463
Because of Atoy.

197
00:10:30,546 --> 00:10:32,131
He's so suspicious of me!

198
00:10:32,214 --> 00:10:34,717
He even introduced me
to Ibyang as her mother, right?

199
00:10:34,800 --> 00:10:36,552
- Mm-hmm.
- But I could see it on his face,

200
00:10:36,636 --> 00:10:37,803
he's full of doubt!

201
00:10:38,471 --> 00:10:40,389
Oh, God. What more does he want?

202
00:10:40,473 --> 00:10:42,892
Didn't you say
you're willing to do a DNA test?

203
00:10:42,975 --> 00:10:45,019
But he didn't entertain that idea.

204
00:10:45,102 --> 00:10:46,228
Oh, why?

205
00:10:46,312 --> 00:10:48,731
I'm willing to give a DNA test.

206
00:10:48,814 --> 00:10:51,776
Madam even prepared samples here, see,

207
00:10:51,859 --> 00:10:54,320
in case they ask me for a DNA test.

208
00:10:55,112 --> 00:10:58,074
[Charmi] And this?
Is this from Ibyang's real mother?

209
00:10:58,699 --> 00:10:59,992
I don't know.

210
00:11:00,076 --> 00:11:01,243
Maybe.

211
00:11:02,411 --> 00:11:05,289
[suspicious music playing]

212
00:11:09,585 --> 00:11:12,671
[music swells]

213
00:11:18,302 --> 00:11:19,804
[music fades]

214
00:11:19,887 --> 00:11:22,014
Oh. Hey, the water!

215
00:11:22,098 --> 00:11:24,392
- Hey! What water?
- The water! Oh, no!

216
00:11:24,475 --> 00:11:26,936
- Did you leave boiling water at home?
- Oh, no. Not that!

217
00:11:27,019 --> 00:11:31,690
The-- The water bottle
I was holding earlier… It's gone.

218
00:11:31,774 --> 00:11:33,859
[sighs] Maybe Atoy took it,

219
00:11:33,943 --> 00:11:37,029
because he plans to have me
DNA tested without me knowing.

220
00:11:37,655 --> 00:11:40,574
Sis, what now? You'll be exposed as fake!

221
00:11:40,658 --> 00:11:42,993
No. We-- We need to find a way
around this.

222
00:11:43,077 --> 00:11:44,912
- Really, sis!
- Ah, we can't leave.

223
00:11:44,995 --> 00:11:46,330
Wait, um…

224
00:11:46,414 --> 00:11:48,749
Wait. I'll ask Madam for help.

225
00:11:48,833 --> 00:11:50,960
[tense music playing]

226
00:11:51,043 --> 00:11:53,462
[line ringing]

227
00:11:54,505 --> 00:11:55,673
Hello, madam?

228
00:11:57,133 --> 00:12:00,511
Madam, there's…
there's just a slight problem.

229
00:12:00,594 --> 00:12:02,847
Please don't be angry.

230
00:12:02,930 --> 00:12:06,725
Um, bu-- but… I already thought of a way.

231
00:12:07,476 --> 00:12:09,603
Yes, I already-- It's okay now.

232
00:12:10,479 --> 00:12:12,231
[in English] What? What do you mean?

233
00:12:12,314 --> 00:12:13,732
[suspicious music playing]

234
00:12:13,816 --> 00:12:16,026
[in English] Okay.
I'll try to get what you need.

235
00:12:17,695 --> 00:12:18,946
Huh?

236
00:12:19,029 --> 00:12:21,031
Why that brand of bottled water?

237
00:12:22,783 --> 00:12:23,868
[in English] Okay.

238
00:12:24,952 --> 00:12:27,121
Just don't get caught.

239
00:12:28,497 --> 00:12:30,583
[music fades]

240
00:12:33,294 --> 00:12:34,837
Ma'am, moscato.

241
00:12:37,381 --> 00:12:39,592
Uh, where's Audrey?

242
00:12:39,675 --> 00:12:41,802
Outside, ma'am. Doing yoga.

243
00:12:41,886 --> 00:12:43,012
[in English] Okay.

244
00:12:43,095 --> 00:12:45,598
[in English] I think maybe you should
bring her some snacks.

245
00:12:45,681 --> 00:12:48,851
Also, do we still have
that Pure Dia water?

246
00:12:48,934 --> 00:12:51,312
I'll check the pantry, ma'am,
if we have it.

247
00:12:51,395 --> 00:12:53,564
- Okay. Give that if ever, okay?
- Okay.

248
00:12:53,647 --> 00:12:54,815
[in English] Thank you.

249
00:12:54,899 --> 00:12:57,818
[suspicious music playing]

250
00:13:03,324 --> 00:13:05,367
[music fades]

251
00:13:11,957 --> 00:13:13,125
Audrey.

252
00:13:15,586 --> 00:13:17,588
[in English] Uh,
Janine is looking for you.

253
00:13:17,671 --> 00:13:19,840
[mysterious music playing]

254
00:13:21,550 --> 00:13:22,760
[Audrey] Janine!

255
00:13:22,843 --> 00:13:27,306
[tense music playing]

256
00:13:34,230 --> 00:13:35,564
[line ringing]

257
00:13:35,648 --> 00:13:38,567
[in English] Hello? Yes, Olga.
I have what you need.

258
00:13:39,860 --> 00:13:41,529
Where will my staff meet you?

259
00:13:41,612 --> 00:13:42,988
[music swells]

260
00:13:43,072 --> 00:13:44,907
[in English] All right. Good.

261
00:13:44,990 --> 00:13:45,824
‪[dramatic sting]

262
00:13:46,742 --> 00:13:48,077
Is it true?

263
00:13:48,827 --> 00:13:50,079
Ibyang's mother showed up?

264
00:13:50,162 --> 00:13:51,038
Mm.

265
00:13:51,121 --> 00:13:54,792
Too bad! I didn't catch her!
I didn't see her!

266
00:13:56,460 --> 00:13:57,962
Too bad.

267
00:14:01,173 --> 00:14:03,926
Why do you look… unhappy?

268
00:14:05,844 --> 00:14:08,264
Ah!

269
00:14:08,347 --> 00:14:11,308
[giggles]

270
00:14:12,142 --> 00:14:13,852
I know.

271
00:14:13,936 --> 00:14:16,313
You don't want Ibyang
taken from you, right?

272
00:14:16,397 --> 00:14:18,357
Oh, no! [chuckles]

273
00:14:18,440 --> 00:14:20,150
'Toy, don't be like that!

274
00:14:20,234 --> 00:14:22,152
Don't be like that, 'Toy!

275
00:14:22,236 --> 00:14:23,863
Of course, I'm happy.

276
00:14:25,698 --> 00:14:28,075
We've wanted this for her
for so long, right?

277
00:14:28,158 --> 00:14:31,871
[pensive music playing]

278
00:14:31,954 --> 00:14:34,123
[sighs] But of course, I need…

279
00:14:36,250 --> 00:14:39,420
I want to make sure
she goes to the right person.

280
00:14:39,503 --> 00:14:41,547
[melancholic music playing]

281
00:14:41,630 --> 00:14:42,882
Oh?

282
00:14:44,717 --> 00:14:46,385
Why do you have doubts about the mother?

283
00:14:49,722 --> 00:14:50,931
[Atoy] A little.

284
00:14:53,559 --> 00:14:54,518
'Son…

285
00:14:55,728 --> 00:14:57,438
I need you to do something.

286
00:14:57,521 --> 00:14:58,647
Hmm?

287
00:15:04,069 --> 00:15:07,197
Go to our contact clinic at the corner.

288
00:15:08,032 --> 00:15:09,116
Give them this.

289
00:15:09,199 --> 00:15:11,702
[suspicious music playing]

290
00:15:11,785 --> 00:15:13,203
This is Olga's specimen sample.

291
00:15:14,538 --> 00:15:17,917
And this, Ibyang's swab specimen.

292
00:15:19,376 --> 00:15:23,047
Request a maternity match test.

293
00:15:23,130 --> 00:15:24,131
Tell them it's rush.

294
00:15:24,715 --> 00:15:27,051
If they agree,
we'll get the result tomorrow.

295
00:15:29,929 --> 00:15:32,514
Okay. Of course, sure.

296
00:15:32,598 --> 00:15:33,849
I got you.

297
00:15:33,933 --> 00:15:36,894
But… Rush? Does that mean right away?

298
00:15:36,977 --> 00:15:39,229
Maybe I can go home first, take a bath?

299
00:15:39,313 --> 00:15:41,690
- 'Son, this is important.
- [in English] Rush, rush.

300
00:15:41,774 --> 00:15:44,234
[music swells]

301
00:15:44,318 --> 00:15:47,529
Okay, okay, okay, okay. All right.

302
00:15:47,613 --> 00:15:49,573
[suspicious music playing]

303
00:15:49,657 --> 00:15:51,492
Rush, you said.

304
00:15:51,575 --> 00:15:54,453
- Who's that?
- Ah--

305
00:15:54,536 --> 00:15:56,664
[clears throat] Hi!

306
00:15:56,747 --> 00:15:59,208
About-- Ah, ah, ah-- Sir Atoy!

307
00:15:59,291 --> 00:16:00,125
Oh?

308
00:16:00,209 --> 00:16:04,254
Uh, I left my shades.
I just came back for them.

309
00:16:04,338 --> 00:16:05,506
Where-- Where could they be?

310
00:16:05,589 --> 00:16:07,424
- Shades? Your shades?
- Yes.

311
00:16:07,508 --> 00:16:08,425
Yes!

312
00:16:10,511 --> 00:16:12,888
Oh?

313
00:16:12,972 --> 00:16:16,475
But you weren't wearing shades earlier.

314
00:16:16,558 --> 00:16:18,852
Excuse me. I'm Faye.

315
00:16:19,436 --> 00:16:21,397
No, I was wearing them earlier.

316
00:16:21,480 --> 00:16:24,525
- No. Are you sure?
- Huh? I wasn't?

317
00:16:25,067 --> 00:16:27,736
Oh, yes! I wasn't, I wasn't.

318
00:16:27,820 --> 00:16:29,405
Okay, I'll leave now.

319
00:16:30,072 --> 00:16:31,240
- Okay.
- I'll leave now. About--

320
00:16:31,323 --> 00:16:33,575
- I'll go home now.
- Okay.

321
00:16:33,659 --> 00:16:36,537
[tense music playing]

322
00:16:41,959 --> 00:16:42,793
‪So, bro…

323
00:16:44,253 --> 00:16:46,171
- Okay.
- Yes, okay.

324
00:16:46,255 --> 00:16:47,506
- You handle it.
- Yes.

325
00:16:47,589 --> 00:16:50,259
- What's that?
- For taxi, food,

326
00:16:50,342 --> 00:16:52,219
payment for the test. It's expensive.

327
00:16:53,053 --> 00:16:54,263
- You'll cash it?
- Oh.

328
00:16:54,346 --> 00:16:56,348
I'll transfer the rest for the test.

329
00:16:56,432 --> 00:16:58,517
- Yes, for the test.
- For the test. You take care of it.

330
00:16:59,727 --> 00:17:01,645
- For snacks, and for--
- Psst.

331
00:17:01,729 --> 00:17:04,398
- [in English] Covert-- Covert ops. Okay?
- [in English] Okay.

332
00:17:04,481 --> 00:17:06,984
- [in English] Okay?
- [in English] Okay. Okay, okay. Yes, sir.

333
00:17:07,568 --> 00:17:08,485
- 'Son.
- [in English] Okay.

334
00:17:08,569 --> 00:17:10,237
[Emerson] I'll handle it.
I'll handle it, 'Toy.

335
00:17:10,779 --> 00:17:12,740
- [in English] Thank you!
- [Emerson] All right!

336
00:17:12,823 --> 00:17:14,408
[sighs]

337
00:17:15,743 --> 00:17:18,120
[music fades]

338
00:17:19,621 --> 00:17:22,249
When we used to live in the bus,

339
00:17:23,083 --> 00:17:25,044
unstable, and…

340
00:17:25,127 --> 00:17:27,629
- [thunder rumbling]
- unsafe with tetanus…

341
00:17:27,713 --> 00:17:30,674
- [thunder rumbling]
- [Ame] <i>One turn, and it's</i>

342
00:17:30,758 --> 00:17:31,675
<i>already the kitchen.</i>

343
00:17:32,885 --> 00:17:34,803
[chuckling softly]

344
00:17:35,387 --> 00:17:38,599
Then we turn around,

345
00:17:38,682 --> 00:17:40,642
it's our bed.

346
00:17:40,726 --> 00:17:43,979
Then we sleep facing each other.

347
00:17:44,730 --> 00:17:46,190
But no moving!

348
00:17:47,566 --> 00:17:50,778
- I almost fell, right?
- Mm-hmm.

349
00:17:50,861 --> 00:17:52,738
But you pulled me back.

350
00:17:52,821 --> 00:17:54,281
[chuckles]

351
00:17:58,118 --> 00:17:59,369
Sis Ame.

352
00:18:01,955 --> 00:18:05,709
Thank you for taking care of me.

353
00:18:07,044 --> 00:18:08,837
- [sentimental music playing]
- [dramatic sting]

354
00:18:09,797 --> 00:18:13,425
[Ibyang] <i>Thank you for loving me.</i>

355
00:18:17,471 --> 00:18:19,139
<i>You became my family.</i>

356
00:18:22,017 --> 00:18:24,895
You were also my only family.

357
00:18:26,396 --> 00:18:28,273
I'm so lucky,

358
00:18:28,899 --> 00:18:31,443
I was given the chance

359
00:18:31,527 --> 00:18:36,323
to be with such a kind and loving child.

360
00:18:37,074 --> 00:18:41,620
[sentimental music playing]

361
00:18:42,788 --> 00:18:44,206
Sis Ame.

362
00:18:45,874 --> 00:18:49,503
Can't you come with me?

363
00:18:51,588 --> 00:18:53,132
[sniffles]

364
00:18:53,215 --> 00:18:54,299
No.

365
00:18:55,217 --> 00:18:58,053
It's your time now to be with your mama.

366
00:18:59,304 --> 00:19:03,058
Even if we don't sleep
side by side anymore,

367
00:19:04,017 --> 00:19:06,145
even if we don't share the same house,

368
00:19:06,770 --> 00:19:08,522
I'll still be your Sister Ame.

369
00:19:09,356 --> 00:19:11,775
And I can still visit you there.

370
00:19:13,569 --> 00:19:15,195
Promise, okay?

371
00:19:16,864 --> 00:19:19,158
Yes, Ibyang. Promise.

372
00:19:21,660 --> 00:19:24,830
[in English] Promise. [inhales] Promise.

373
00:19:29,418 --> 00:19:32,462
Can I hug you a little longer?

374
00:19:35,674 --> 00:19:37,843
I haven't bathed yet.

375
00:19:39,386 --> 00:19:41,096
That's okay.

376
00:19:41,180 --> 00:19:46,518
[sobs] I want to keep your scent with me.

377
00:19:46,602 --> 00:19:48,770
And here, on our bed.

378
00:19:49,897 --> 00:19:53,192
So, when you're with your mama,

379
00:19:53,275 --> 00:19:55,694
I won't feel too sad.

380
00:19:57,070 --> 00:19:58,363
Hmm?

381
00:19:58,447 --> 00:20:00,699
[pensive music playing]

382
00:20:03,702 --> 00:20:05,037
Sis Ame.

383
00:20:05,120 --> 00:20:07,456
[sentimental music playing]

384
00:20:07,539 --> 00:20:09,166
I'll miss you.

385
00:20:12,044 --> 00:20:13,503
What about me?

386
00:20:15,756 --> 00:20:18,425
But it's okay because…

387
00:20:19,343 --> 00:20:20,928
I know…

388
00:20:22,930 --> 00:20:25,140
that you'll be happier there.

389
00:20:26,808 --> 00:20:29,311
That your identity will be complete.

390
00:20:39,488 --> 00:20:41,240
[music fades]

391
00:20:41,323 --> 00:20:42,866
Sister Ame won't be there.

392
00:20:43,909 --> 00:20:44,952
[sobs]

393
00:20:45,744 --> 00:20:47,246
Be good there, okay.

394
00:20:47,329 --> 00:20:52,417
[sentimental music playing]

395
00:21:08,475 --> 00:21:09,977
Hey! What?

396
00:21:10,060 --> 00:21:11,561
Hasn't Martina's man arrived yet?

397
00:21:11,645 --> 00:21:13,105
Emerson might leave.

398
00:21:13,188 --> 00:21:14,356
They said he's on his way.

399
00:21:16,817 --> 00:21:19,444
It's taking too long.
He should've been here earlier.

400
00:21:20,028 --> 00:21:21,321
- [knocks]
- [gasps]

401
00:21:22,906 --> 00:21:24,283
- [gasps]
- Are you Olga?

402
00:21:24,866 --> 00:21:27,577
Yes, that's me.
We've been waiting for you, sir.

403
00:21:27,661 --> 00:21:29,746
Madam Martina sent this.

404
00:21:29,830 --> 00:21:30,831
Here's what you need.

405
00:21:30,914 --> 00:21:33,250
[suspicious music playing]

406
00:21:33,333 --> 00:21:37,379
Perfect! Wait! Don't leave yet.
I still need you.

407
00:21:37,462 --> 00:21:38,880
Let me borrow some clothes, sis.

408
00:21:38,964 --> 00:21:39,965
Oh, here.

409
00:21:40,048 --> 00:21:42,592
Perfect, I brought a costume for you.

410
00:21:43,927 --> 00:21:45,929
Sir, listen carefully.

411
00:21:46,013 --> 00:21:47,597
This role is crucial.

412
00:21:47,681 --> 00:21:49,224
You need to understand it well.

413
00:21:49,308 --> 00:21:50,767
Here's the plan.

414
00:21:50,851 --> 00:21:53,270
We'll go inside that tailoring shop.

415
00:21:54,104 --> 00:21:57,774
Then we'll pretend to be a wealthy couple.

416
00:21:57,858 --> 00:21:59,901
You'll act like you're buying,

417
00:21:59,985 --> 00:22:01,570
and when he measures you,

418
00:22:01,653 --> 00:22:03,113
you need to distract him.

419
00:22:03,196 --> 00:22:05,115
- Okay? Clear?
- Clear, madam.

420
00:22:11,913 --> 00:22:13,957
[man] Excuse me.
I'd like to have a suit tailored.

421
00:22:14,041 --> 00:22:15,792
[sneaky music playing]

422
00:22:15,876 --> 00:22:17,294
Ah, sorry.

423
00:22:17,377 --> 00:22:20,756
Maybe… you can come back later,

424
00:22:20,839 --> 00:22:23,550
because I have an errand.
I'm closing the shop now.

425
00:22:23,633 --> 00:22:25,010
Oh, no.

426
00:22:26,053 --> 00:22:28,263
So, you refuse clients?

427
00:22:28,346 --> 00:22:30,015
[in English] That's bad for business.

428
00:22:31,183 --> 00:22:32,225
[sighs] Too bad.

429
00:22:32,309 --> 00:22:36,730
We were going to order an entire entourage
for my child's wedding.

430
00:22:37,314 --> 00:22:40,150
Well, if you don't want to,
then forget it. Let's go, honey.

431
00:22:40,233 --> 00:22:42,778
Ah, ah-- No, no. Wait, wait.

432
00:22:42,861 --> 00:22:44,696
You didn't say so.

433
00:22:44,780 --> 00:22:47,574
Um, this will be quick.
Let me measure your husband first.

434
00:22:47,657 --> 00:22:49,451
I'll start with him. Sir, come here.

435
00:22:49,534 --> 00:22:52,871
- We're in a hurry too--
- You didn't say so.

436
00:22:52,954 --> 00:22:55,165
Here, sir. Ah, let's remove that.

437
00:22:56,083 --> 00:22:57,918
[Emerson] Ah, there.

438
00:22:58,001 --> 00:23:00,003
[in English] Neck, that.

439
00:23:00,087 --> 00:23:01,713
[in English] Armhole.

440
00:23:07,427 --> 00:23:10,013
Good thing you thought
of having your suit made here

441
00:23:10,097 --> 00:23:11,807
and not at Sir Delfin's.

442
00:23:11,890 --> 00:23:15,143
Yes, because…
I didn't like the vibes there.

443
00:23:15,811 --> 00:23:17,813
- [Emerson] Oh, really?
- [Olga] Mmm-hmm.

444
00:23:17,896 --> 00:23:20,190
Ah, good thing you came here.

445
00:23:20,273 --> 00:23:21,358
[giggles]

446
00:23:21,441 --> 00:23:23,693
- Will this take long?
- [in English] Okay.

447
00:23:23,777 --> 00:23:26,780
- Okay. All right.
- [Olga] Done?

448
00:23:26,863 --> 00:23:28,990
Yes, um…

449
00:23:29,741 --> 00:23:35,622
Just leave your contact number

450
00:23:35,705 --> 00:23:39,376
so I can call you with the details.

451
00:23:39,459 --> 00:23:41,419
Oh, no. We'll just come back.

452
00:23:41,503 --> 00:23:42,796
- Okay, okay.
- [Olga] All right, all right.

453
00:23:42,879 --> 00:23:44,047
- [in English] Thank you.
- [Emerson, in English] Okay.

454
00:23:44,131 --> 00:23:45,090
- Yes, yes.
- Thanks.

455
00:23:45,173 --> 00:23:46,299
- Thank you.
- [in English] Let's go, hon.

456
00:23:46,383 --> 00:23:48,176
[tense music playing]

457
00:23:49,052 --> 00:23:50,303
Ah, jackpot.

458
00:24:04,025 --> 00:24:06,778
[in English] Okay, okay.

459
00:24:16,371 --> 00:24:17,330
So, that's it.

460
00:24:18,039 --> 00:24:22,169
Miss Cita said
Ibyang's RL mother arrived!

461
00:24:22,752 --> 00:24:24,087
RL, RL.

462
00:24:24,671 --> 00:24:25,630
What's RL?

463
00:24:25,714 --> 00:24:28,175
RL, "real life"! In real life!

464
00:24:28,258 --> 00:24:30,886
There, see! Miss Siony is very good!

465
00:24:30,969 --> 00:24:34,055
- Always updated with…
- The latest terms.

466
00:24:34,139 --> 00:24:36,808
- [man] Yes.
- That's why Miss Siony always looks good.

467
00:24:36,892 --> 00:24:39,352
- Of course, That's Miss Siony.
- [man] Miss Siony.

468
00:24:39,436 --> 00:24:40,604
[sneaky music playing]

469
00:24:40,687 --> 00:24:42,147
[chuckling]

470
00:24:42,230 --> 00:24:44,024
- Hey, come eat!
- Oh, Karla.

471
00:24:44,107 --> 00:24:45,567
Come, sit here first.

472
00:24:46,359 --> 00:24:48,153
Have you heard the news?

473
00:24:48,236 --> 00:24:51,114
Yes. Sis Ame texted me.

474
00:24:51,198 --> 00:24:54,576
It's good that Ibyang
is with her real mother.

475
00:24:54,659 --> 00:24:55,827
Ah!

476
00:24:55,911 --> 00:24:57,495
What if Ibyang leaves?

477
00:24:57,579 --> 00:24:59,748
What about Brother Atoy?

478
00:25:00,332 --> 00:25:02,250
[T-Bak] Then he'll go solo in life!

479
00:25:02,959 --> 00:25:06,546
No. Sis Ame is still there,
and Miss Cita too.

480
00:25:06,630 --> 00:25:09,716
Oh, but Cita's gone! She resigned.

481
00:25:09,799 --> 00:25:12,802
Why isn't your mom there, Karla?

482
00:25:12,886 --> 00:25:14,763
[suspicious music playing]

483
00:25:14,846 --> 00:25:17,641
Do she and Atoy have a problem, child?

484
00:25:19,142 --> 00:25:20,977
Um, well-- [clears throat]

485
00:25:21,061 --> 00:25:22,270
No, it's…

486
00:25:22,354 --> 00:25:26,483
Miss Cita, she just went on vacation.

487
00:25:26,566 --> 00:25:29,736
Mm-hmm. Of course,
she has to relax when there's time.

488
00:25:29,819 --> 00:25:30,987
Yes.

489
00:25:31,071 --> 00:25:34,115
You know, Atoy should take a vacation too.

490
00:25:34,199 --> 00:25:36,409
Well, if you get the chance,

491
00:25:36,493 --> 00:25:39,996
any of you, check on Atoy.

492
00:25:40,080 --> 00:25:43,833
Even if we know him as strong,
brave, steadfast,

493
00:25:43,917 --> 00:25:47,504
he also feels pain from losing Ibyang.

494
00:25:47,587 --> 00:25:51,341
As far as I know,
he treated the child like his own.

495
00:25:51,424 --> 00:25:52,842
That's true, Father.

496
00:25:52,926 --> 00:25:56,012
[melancholic music playing]

497
00:26:05,522 --> 00:26:07,983
[pensive music playing]

498
00:26:09,567 --> 00:26:12,279
[phone ringing]

499
00:26:16,533 --> 00:26:17,784
Oh, 'Tols?

500
00:26:18,368 --> 00:26:20,370
[Emerson on the phone]
<i>'Toy, I just want to know…</i>

501
00:26:20,912 --> 00:26:23,915
<i>has the DNA test result</i>
<i>been emailed to you?</i>

502
00:26:23,999 --> 00:26:25,542
<i>They're sending it today.</i>

503
00:26:27,043 --> 00:26:28,295
Yes, it arrived.

504
00:26:30,213 --> 00:26:31,506
Positive, Emerson.

505
00:26:32,340 --> 00:26:33,925
She really is the mother.

506
00:26:34,009 --> 00:26:35,051
[pensive music playing]

507
00:26:35,135 --> 00:26:36,845
[Emerson on the phone] <i>Oh, there you go.</i>

508
00:26:36,928 --> 00:26:39,222
<i>You said you'd be happy, right?</i>

509
00:26:41,891 --> 00:26:44,185
Okay then. We'll talk later.

510
00:26:44,269 --> 00:26:45,729
[music fades]

511
00:26:45,812 --> 00:26:47,022
[clears throat]

512
00:26:48,440 --> 00:26:49,482
[footsteps approaching]

513
00:26:50,066 --> 00:26:51,484
[knocks]

514
00:26:51,568 --> 00:26:52,986
Hello!

515
00:26:53,069 --> 00:26:56,740
Oh. Hello, Atoy! I'm here to fetch Ibyang.

516
00:26:56,823 --> 00:26:58,158
Yes.

517
00:26:59,492 --> 00:27:01,286
Uh, she's just…

518
00:27:01,369 --> 00:27:03,079
Where's Olga? Why--

519
00:27:03,163 --> 00:27:04,622
- Uh…
- [Atoy] Isn't she fetching her?

520
00:27:04,706 --> 00:27:07,083
Olga is at home, cleaning.

521
00:27:07,167 --> 00:27:09,753
Preparing for Ibyang's arrival.

522
00:27:09,836 --> 00:27:11,296
Will Ibyang take long?

523
00:27:11,379 --> 00:27:14,007
Ah, no. She's ready too.

524
00:27:14,090 --> 00:27:15,759
- I'll just call her.
- Okay.

525
00:27:15,842 --> 00:27:18,720
[melodramatic music playing]

526
00:27:18,803 --> 00:27:21,097
[electronic blipping]

527
00:27:22,182 --> 00:27:24,976
- [tense music playing]
- [electronic blipping]

528
00:27:29,397 --> 00:27:31,608
It's really hard to fight loneliness,
isn't it?

529
00:27:31,691 --> 00:27:34,986
[Atoy] <i>Think about it, just recently,</i>
<i>Ibyang came into my life.</i>

530
00:27:35,070 --> 00:27:36,780
<i>Then, my family.</i>

531
00:27:36,863 --> 00:27:38,281
<i>And now they're all gone.</i>

532
00:27:38,365 --> 00:27:39,908
They came quickly, but…

533
00:27:39,991 --> 00:27:41,326
were taken from me just as fast.

534
00:27:41,409 --> 00:27:42,702
UP NEXT

535
00:27:42,786 --> 00:27:44,913
[in English] I was ordered
by Colonel Mercado to meet you

536
00:27:44,996 --> 00:27:46,331
and deliver his directives.

537
00:27:46,998 --> 00:27:48,875
[goon actor 1] The job could've been easy,

538
00:27:48,958 --> 00:27:50,752
but they're making it hard.

539
00:27:50,835 --> 00:27:53,922
Exactly. Olga is such a headache.

540
00:27:54,506 --> 00:27:55,965
[goon actor 1] We'll kill her anyway.

541
00:27:56,049 --> 00:27:57,342
[gasps]

542
00:27:57,425 --> 00:27:59,260
[music swells]

543
00:27:59,344 --> 00:28:00,595
Mama!

544
00:28:01,721 --> 00:28:03,014
[groans]

545
00:28:04,641 --> 00:28:06,476
[objects clanging and clattering]

546
00:28:07,102 --> 00:28:07,977
[in English] Hey! Cut!

547
00:28:08,645 --> 00:28:10,271
[director] What's happening here?

548
00:28:10,355 --> 00:28:11,523
[music swells]

549
00:28:11,606 --> 00:28:14,234
[gunshots]

550
00:28:14,317 --> 00:28:17,237
[security officer, in English]
We used AI to see what he might look like.

551
00:28:17,320 --> 00:28:22,283
I want you to find out
everything about this man.

552
00:28:22,367 --> 00:28:24,411
[grunting and groaning]

553
00:28:25,870 --> 00:28:26,996
[gunshots]

554
00:28:27,080 --> 00:28:29,791
["Mr. Tailor" playing]

555
00:28:33,086 --> 00:28:34,796
♪ <i>Fix it</i> ♪

556
00:28:34,879 --> 00:28:36,339
Subtitle translation by: Rachel C. Arias
